WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.362
Step five shows the reader refusing.

2
00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:05.578
You build a reader for the
inventory task in G C C,

3
00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:09.537
on the fake, and ask it for the
Conditional Access policies.

4
00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:12.915
That call isn't declared for the
inventory task, so it throws,

5
00:00:12.915 --> 00:00:16.225
and tells you to add it to the
call list with its permission.

6
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:20.863
Then you ask for a cloud called
G C C High, with capital letters.

7
00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:26.784
The names are case-sensitive on
purpose, so that's an unknown cloud,

8
00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:30.951
and it throws too: use global,
G C C, G C C High or D O D.

9
00:00:30.951 --> 00:00:32.462
There's no default cloud.

10
00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:37.662
Step six runs the whole test suite,
three hundred thirty tests, and all pass.

11
00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:42.225
Then delete the output folder, because it
names the fixture's privileged holders.

12
00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:46.870
Pester prints its summary on several
lines; the slide shows it on one.
